 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a pause that grows by 2 seconds before each
+retry: 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds. When the fifth attempt times out too, the capture fails with `GatewayTimeout`. The
+member waits on the confirmation page through the pauses, up to 20 seconds longer than one attempt.
+
+The gateway answers slowly every Friday from 17:00 to 19:00, its peak. Captures were tried up to 3 times back to back,
+within one second, so all three landed in the same slow minute: one Friday left 58 pantry orders confirmed but never
+charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next morning. Replaying that
+Friday's timeouts against the gateway's sandbox with 5 attempts spaced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart, 57 of the 58
+went through. Switching gateways was ruled out while the contract runs, to December 2026. The longer wait on the
+confirmation page was accepted as cheaper than captures by hand.
 
